        "original_id": "20ef92a2-ade8-5d25-9072-c521beb9b1cb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Songs: Mmm Papi, La Isla Bonita, Whiplash, Rock Me In\n- People: Madonna, Patrick Leonard, Bruce Gaitsch, Selena Gomez & the Scene\n- Albums: True Blue\n- Concepts: Latin pop influence, songwriting, production\n\nFacts:\n- In 1986, Madonna released \"La Isla Bonita\" on her third studio album \"True Blue\".\n- In 1987, Madonna's song \"La Isla Bonita\" was noted as a Latin pop song and later served as a comparison point for \"Mmm Papi\".\n- Madonna and Patrick Leonard co-wrote and co-produced \"La Isla Bonita\", and Bruce Gaitsch contributed additional songwriting.\n- \"Mmm Papi\" is noted for having a Latin pop influence similar to Madonna's \"La Isla Bonita\".\n- The same writers together wrote the songs \"Mmm Papi\", \"Rock Me In\", and \"Whiplash\" for Selena Gomez & the Scene.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
